nk:href=\"#CrimsonText-Italic-120\"></use>\n     </g>\n    </g>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"line2d_1\">\n    <path clip-path=\"url(#p9449216721)\" d=\"M 113.89394 34.887397 \nL 223.645253 254.390022 \nL 223.645253 254.390022 \n\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-linecap:square;stroke-width:2.3;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"line2d_2\">\n    <path clip-path=\"url(#p9449216721)\" d=\"M 37.782876 101.239284 \nL 242.567893 254.828046 \nL 242.567893 254.828046 \n\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-linecap:square;stroke-width:2.3;\"></path>\n   </g>\n  </g>\n </g>\n <defs>\n  <clipPath id=\"p9449216721\">\n   <rect height=\"260.82\" width=\"268.898496\" x=\"7.2\" y=\"7.2\"></rect>\n  </clipPath>\n </defs>\n</svg>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for graph of a system of 2 lines\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>For the first line in the system:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>The line slants sharply down from left to right.</li>\n<li>The line passes through the following points:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>(0 comma 3)</li>\n<li>(4 comma negative 5)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>For the second line in the system:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>The line slants gradually down from left to right.</li>\n<li>The line passes through the following points:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>(0 comma negative 2)</li>\n<li>(4 comma negative 5)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The graph of a system of linear equations is shown. What is the solution&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> to the system?</p>","keys":["8a156913-163a-4929-9aa1-fa972abfc929"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"8a156913-163a-4929-9aa1-fa972abfc929","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis 4 comma negative 5 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"},{"id":"2c2a7b0f-fa1a-468e-aded-52b17f5803fb","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma 3 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"},{"id":"db52eb4f-2521-434e-904a-c8c82f0d3dbf","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma negative 2 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"},{"id":"11095b73-a172-4391-b13c-10bb33bc9445","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis negative 2 comma 3 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. The solution to this system of linear equations is represented by the point that lies on both lines shown, or the point of intersection of the two lines. According to the graph, the point of intersection occurs when <math alttext=\"x equals 4\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>4</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"y equals negative 5\"><mrow>\n<mi>y</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mn>5</mn>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>, or at the point <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 4 comma negative 5 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Therefore, the solution&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> to the system is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 4 comma negative 5 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","externalid":"fef8ab08-2a09-4477-9b15-1ed3a9fc0ac6","correct_answer":["A"]},"createDate":1743430554989,"updateDate":1743430554989}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1743430554989, 1743430554989),
    ($SATQ$cd33b015$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$026034-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.D.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Systems of two linear equations in two variables$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<div class="stimulus_reference"><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/cd33b015/img_000_ff6de586.png" alt="Equation 1: x plus y, equals 20."></span><p><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/cd33b015/img_001_a9cc3c90.png" alt="Equation 2: 2 times, open parenthesis, x plus y, close parenthesis, plus 3 y, equals 85."></span></p></div>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">If <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/cd33b015/img_002_7284e904.png" alt="the ordered pair x comma y "></span> is the solution to the given system of equations, what is the value of <span class="italic">y</span> ?</p>
