ML" alttext="negative 84 equals negative 84"><mo>−</mo><mn>84</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>84</mn></math>, which is true. Additionally, the table in choice A shows that when <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x equals 4"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals 28"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>28</mn></math>. Substituting these values into the given equation yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="7 left parenthesis 4 right parenthesis minus 4 left parenthesis 28 right parenthesis equals negative 84"><mn>7</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>84</mn></math>, or&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="negative 84 equals negative 84"><mo>−</mo><mn>84</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>84</mn></math>, which is true. Finally, the table in choice A shows that when <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x equals 8"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals 35"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>35</mn></math>. Substituting these values into the given equation yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="7 left parenthesis 8 right parenthesis minus 4 left parenthesis 35 right parenthesis equals negative 84"><mn>7</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>35</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>84</mn></math>, or&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="negative 84 equals negative 84"><mo>−</mo><mn>84</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>84</mn></math>, which is true. Therefore, the table in choice A gives three values of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> and their corresponding values of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math>.</p>
